\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{88466b3}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The cap on a warm session is now a property of the engine a session belongs to: 4 MiB for the machine, 16 MiB for every other engine. \code{\verb~|-X session-mib~} or a run default of the primary engine's provider wins over both; the launcher applies such run defaults under the command line. A unit that runs longer than 20 ms returns the unstarted rest of its worker's claim while it is still running. Measured with the machine in the native image at \code{\verb~|-O3~} in the arena-shaped container, median of three: reachability with 8 workers 6.50 to 4.66 s wall (-28 \%) at 8.49 to 8.59 s CPU, with 4 workers 8.31 to 4.08 s (-51 \%); Init, Std and con-leche show no difference beyond noise. Mathlib with the machine and 8 workers peaks at 2,815 MiB RSS in batch mode and 3,387 MiB pipelined. Published with 100 tests, 97 run green and 3 opt-in.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-driver/README.md}, \src{rlvm-main/README.md}. Commit \commit{88466b3}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE).}
